G={"title":"Present Simple vs Present Continuous","meaning":"Present Simple describes routines; Present Continuous describes actions around now.","use":"Choose by meaning and signal words, not by memorising one form.","form":"routine: subject + base verb; now: subject + am/is/are + verb-ing","explanation_en":"Use Present Simple for habits and schedules. Use Present Continuous for temporary actions happening now or today.","explanation_ar":"نستخدم المضارع البسيط للعادات والجداول، والمستمر لما يحدث الآن أو بصورة مؤقتة اليوم.","examples":("I usually study after dinner.","I am studying at the library today.","Does she work on Thursday?","They aren’t playing now."),"common_mistakes":("I am usually study → I usually study","She studies now → She is studying now","Does he working? → Is he working?"),"comparison":"usually/every day → Simple; now/today/at the moment → Continuous","quick_check":"Maha usually walks, but today she is taking the bus.","tips":("اسأل: هل هو روتين أم حدث الآن؟","أفعال like وknow لا تستخدم غالبًا بصيغة continuous في هذا المستوى.")}
